# ── Committed vector-DB artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# db/ is intentionally tracked (see .gitignore) because the deployed backend
# has no persistent volume and needs the pre-built Chroma index in the image.
#
# But these are large binaries — chroma.sqlite3 alone is ~31MB. Left to its own
# devices git will sniff them, attempt textual diffs, and try three-way merges
# that can only ever produce a corrupt index. `binary` (= -text -diff) stops
# the diffing and any EOL munging; `-merge` makes a conflict here an explicit
# "pick one side" instead of a silently mangled database file.
db/chroma.sqlite3   binary -merge
db/**/*.bin         binary -merge
db/**/*.pickle      binary -merge
